  "confidence": 0.96,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "polarity",
      "components": ["D2"],
      "pins": ["D2.1", "D2.2"],
      "nets": ["+5V", "Net-(D2-A)"],
      "observed": "D2 is connected with its cathode (pin 1, K) on the +5V rail and its anode (pin 2, A) on the servo power rail Net-(D2-A).",
      "expected": "D2 should be oriented from +5V into the servo power rail, i.e. anode on +5V and cathode on the servo rail feeding J3/J8 pin 2 and C1-C4.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "D2 | PMEG3030EP Schottky, schematic note \"3A 360mV\" | Diode from `+5V` into the servo power rail (feeding J3/J8 pin 2 and the C1–C4 bank), selected for a low (≈360 mV @ 3A) forward drop."},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"2\") (name \"+5V\") ... (node (ref \"D2\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"K\") ...))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"33\") (name \"Net-(D2-A)\") ... (node (ref \"D2\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") ...) (node (ref \"J3\") (pin \"2\") ...) (node (ref \"J8\") (pin \"2\") ...))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(libpart (lib \"Device\") (part \"D_Schottky\") ... (pins (pin (num \"1\") (name \"K\") ...) (pin (num \"2\") (name \"A\") ...))"}
      ],
      "impact": "The servo power rail is isolated from the +5V supply instead of being powered through D2, so PWM or serial servos connected to J3/J8 would not receive their intended 5V power. If the servo rail were externally powered, the reversed diode could also allow current to feed back toward the +5V rail.",
      "confidence": 0.96
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist shows D2 installed backwards relative to the specification: its cathode is tied to +5V and its anode to the servo rail, preventing the intended +5V-to-servo-rail diode drop and leaving the servo power rail unpowered."
}

